// FinalHypothesis is one row of the belief state a run ended at. It carries only what scoring a
// run needs — which hypothesis, how confident, which published bucket, what status — and not the
// evidence behind it, which is already in the trajectory's own records.
//
// Phase 7 Track F added it so that calibration is computable from a layer-1 recording alone. A
// trajectory records the judgments a run applied but not the posterior they produced, so a corpus
// of recordings scored zero hypotheses and the reliability table said, correctly but uselessly,
// that it could not measure anything. The posterior is a function of the judgments and the
// published likelihood-ratio table, so recording it costs one small repeated field and makes the
// per-pull-request calibration gate real.
